ca's deaths have been  disproportionately high in black  communities revealing long-standing  health and socio-economic disparities  Zenobia is now focusing her grief on the  urgent need for protections for  essential workers she wants them to be  better rewarded than lolani this is her  final paycheck 20 dollars in 63 cents  and you received that after she died yes  for all that she has done she should  have been getting paid way more money  six years and this is all you get as the  daughter of a military family lolani now  shares her final resting place with  fallen heroes in Arlington National  Cemetery  this new invisible enemy has now claimed  more American lives than the Vietnam  Gulf Iraq and Afghanistan wars combined  for a nation living in isolation it's  perhaps harder to share a collective  sense of grief even harder to tune out  the ongoing political noise of this  crisis but make no mistake America is  engulfed in tragedy with no cure or  vaccine this is not the end Amanda  Walker Sky News Washington
 

